#
# An aggregator whose include DOES resolve and whose child parses cleanly, but
# whose transitive closure contributes ZERO cases because the child declares an
# empty `mf:entries ()`. The aggregator itself is well-formed; only the recursion
# into the child catches it, and the error must name the CHILD, not this file.
#
# An empty `rdf:List` is `rdf:nil`, which carries no `rdf:first`, so the loader's
# `rdf:rest*/rdf:first` walk sees exactly what it sees for a manifest with no
# `mf:entries` at all — which is why the empty case is detected by a separate
# property-presence query and diagnosed in its own words.
@prefix mf: <http://www.w3.org/2001/sw/DataAccess/tests/test-manifest#> .

<> a mf:Manifest ;
    mf:include ( <empty-group/manifest.ttl> ) .
